 "post": {
  "title": "3 Reasons Your Mind Goes Blank #shorts",
  "description": "1) Radvansky et al. (2011): walking through a doorway causes more forgetting than the same distance within a room (an event boundary). 2) Brenner (1973), the next-in-line effect: people recall least of what was said just before their own turn. 3) Sparrow et al. (2011): people who expected information to be saved on a computer remembered it less. #psychology #shorts #memory",
